            <ArticleTitle>Carotid-cavernous sinus fistula presenting as a posterior fossa mass. Case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>585-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors report a case in which trigeminal neuralgia and hearing loss developed 14 years after a severe head injury. Arteriography demonstrated a carotid-cavernous sinus fistula producing a large venous mass in the posterior fossa.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
